,"linkLabel":"📰 Public PIR benchmark","subTarget":"pir","style":"link"},{"id":"04c0d64d-4fc3-5400-8d43-81b8f8338b45","cellValue":"tab","linkTarget":"parameter","linkLabel":"🔮 Expected downtime","subTarget":"planner","style":"link"},{"id":"e9f29d98-f0e4-5fbc-9527-2ea254bbef27","cellValue":"tab","linkTarget":"parameter","linkLabel":"❤️ Data health","subTarget":"health","style":"link"},{"id":"4234f74b-f119-5830-803f-e579f426d2c7","cellValue":"tab","linkTarget":"parameter","linkLabel":"ℹ️ About, method and caveats","subTarget":"method","style":"link"}]},"name":"tabs"},{"type":12,"content":{"version":"NotebookGroup/1.0","groupType":"editable","title":"Overview","items":[{"type":1,"content":{"json":"**What this page shows**

A quick summary of the problems and maintenance Azure has reported for your subscriptions in the selected time range, and how much your resources were actually unavailable.

**How to read it**

- Start with **What needs your attention**: a short checklist. Green tick = fine, amber warning = take a look, red = act, blue info = for your information.
- **Unplanned events** are Azure incidents that nobody scheduled. **Planned maintenance** is work Azure announced in advance.
- **Event time open** (exposure) is how long events were officially open. It is *not* how long your resources were down.
- **Observed downtime** is the number of minutes your resources were reported *Unavailable*. Time you caused yourself (for example stopping a VM) is left out.
- **Observed availability** is the share of time your resources were up, from that downtime and the number of resources you have.
- Each event is counted once, even if it affected several services or regions. Use the filters at the top to narrow the view.
- The small **line under a number** is the weekly trend across the selected time range.","style":"info"},"name":"ov-desc"},{"type":3,"content":{"version":"KqlItem/1.0","query":"let win_days = toint(datetime_diff("day", {TimeRange:end}, {TimeRange:start}));
let es = AzMaintenance_EventServices({IncludeSynthetic})
    | where impact_start_utc between ({TimeRange:start} .. {TimeRange:end})
    | where '*' in ({Subscriptions}) or subscription_id in ({Subscriptions})
    | where '*' in ({Category}) or category in ({Category})
    | where '*' in ({Service}) or service in ({Service})
    | where '*' in ({Region}) or region in ({Region});
let avail = AzMaintenance_Availability(win_days, {IncludeUserInitiated}, {IncludeSynthetic})
    | where '*' in ({Category}) or category in ({Category})
    | where '*' in ({Service}) or service_name in ({Service});
let iv = AzMaintenance_ResourceIntervals({IncludeSynthetic})
    | where '*' in ({Subscriptions}) or subscription_id in ({Subscriptions})
    | where '*' in ({Category}) or category in ({Category})
    | where '*' in ({Service}) or service_name in ({Service})
    | where end_utc > {TimeRange:start} and start_utc < {TimeRange:end}
    | where {IncludeUserInitiated} or not(user_initiated);
let open_u = toscalar(es | where is_open and class == "Unplanned" | summarize dcount(tracking_id));
let down_now = toscalar(iv | where state =~ "Unavailable" and is_open and not(stale_open) | summarize dcount(resource_id));
let recent = toscalar(es | where class == "Unplanned" and impact_start_utc > ago(7d) | summarize dcount(tracking_id));
let soon = toscalar(AzMaintenance_Planned({IncludeSynthetic}) | where upcoming and window_start_utc < now() + 14d | summarize dcount(tracking_id));
let stale_src = toscalar(AzMaintenance_DataHealth({IncludeSynthetic}) | where section == "ingest" and status == "STALE" | summarize count());
datatable(order: int)[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
| extend status = case(order == 1, iff(open_u > 0, "bad", "good"),
                       order == 2, iff(down_now > 0, "bad", "good"),
                       order == 3, iff(recent > 0, "warn", "good"),
                       order == 4, iff(soon > 0, "info", "good"),
                       iff(stale_src > 0, "warn", "good")),
         message = case(order == 1, iff(open_u > 0, strcat(open_u, " Azure incident(s) still open"), "No Azure incidents are open right now"),
                        order == 2, iff(down_now > 0, strcat(down_now, " resource(s) unavailable right now"), "All tracked resources are available"),
                        order == 3, iff(recent > 0, strcat(recent, " unplanned event(s) in the last 7 days"), "No unplanned events in the last 7 days"),
                        order == 4, iff(soon > 0, strcat(soon, " planned maintenance notice(s) in the next 14 days"), "No planned maintenance in the next 14 days"),
                        iff(stale_src > 0, strcat(stale_src, " data source(s) have not reported in 36 hours"), "All data sources are reporting")),
         detail = case(order == 1, iff(open_u > 0, "See the longest events on the Timeline tab", "Nothing to do"),
                       order == 2, iff(down_now > 0, "See the Resources tab for which ones", "Nothing to do"),
                       order == 3, iff(recent > 0, "See the Timeline tab for details", "Nothing to do"),
                       order == 4, iff(soon > 0, "See the Planned maintenance tab for dates and services", "Nothing to do"),
                       iff(stale_src > 0, "Numbers may be out of date: see the Data health tab", "Numbers are up to date"))
| project order, status, message, detail
| order by order asc
